@startuml ethernet_frer_Sequence_Diagram

skinparam sequenceArrowThickness 2
skinparam backgroundColor #FAFAFA

title Ethernet FRER (IEEE 802.1CB Frame Replication and Elimination) Example Project

actor "Sender App\n(hal_entry)" as SAPP
participant "Sender FRER EP\n(frer_example_run)" as SEP
participant "Sender L3 Switch\n(r_layer3_switch)" as SSW
participant "Receiver L3 Switch\n(r_layer3_switch)" as RSW
participant "Receiver FRER EP\n(frer_example_run)" as REP
actor "Receiver App\n(hal_entry)" as RAPP
participant "Host PC\n(2x TeraTerm session)" as PC

legend top left
**loop**  : Repeated every cycle/interval
**alt**   : Branch on condition
**opt**   : Optional / conditional
**note**  : Key design explanation
endlegend

== Sender: System Initialization ==

SAPP -> SEP: frer_example_run()
SEP -> SSW: frer_open()\n-> R_LAYER3_SWITCH_Open(g_layer3_switch0)
SSW --> SEP: FSP_SUCCESS
note over SSW #FFF9C4
This Sender never needs the RMAC promiscuous-
mode fix the Receiver's own frer_open() applies:
that fix only matters for a board classifying
frames arriving from an external port by a
non-local destination MAC.
end note

SEP -> SEP: wait for ETH0 + ETH1 link UP\n(30 s timeout -- generous for manual\ntwo-board debug-attach pacing)
SEP -> PC: console: "[FRER] ETH0 link: UP  ETH1 link: UP (after N ms)"

SEP -> SSW: frer_configure_stream()\n-> ConfigureTable() + AddTableEntry()
note over SEP, SSW #D4E6F1
One L3 entry, destination_ports = Port0|Port1.
Each port gets its own update config
(p_mac_destination_address, r_tag_update_mode set
to ALWAYS_ADD, sequence_number_generation_enable
set to true) so the two member streams end up
on distinct destination MACs with independent
hardware sequence counters.
end note
SSW --> SEP: FSP_SUCCESS

SEP -> SSW: frer_tx_queue_create()\n-> R_LAYER3_SWITCH_CreateDescriptorQueue()
note over SEP, SSW #FFF9C4
Deliberately NOT pre-primed: s_tx_desc[] already
starts zero-initialised. Pre-populating every
slot up front was tried and found to break the
very first real send, since it advances the
driver's internal tail index before any real
frame exists.
end note
SSW --> SEP: FSP_SUCCESS
SEP -> PC: console: "[FRER] L3 entries: 1  TX queue index: N"

== Receiver: System Initialization (independent boot, other board) ==

RAPP -> REP: frer_example_run()
REP -> RSW: frer_open()\n-> R_LAYER3_SWITCH_Open(g_layer3_switch0)
RSW --> REP: FSP_SUCCESS
REP -> RSW: R_RMAC0/1->MRAFC = 0x03C703C7UL
note over RSW #FFF9C4
Required here (not on the Sender): frames
addressed to the replicated stream's MACs
(...0A/...0B) are not this board's own port
MAC, so without this promiscuous-mode fix
RMAC's receive filter drops them before they
ever reach L3-table classification.
end note

REP -> RSW: frer_rx_queue_create(Port0)\nfrer_rx_queue_create(Port1)
note over REP, RSW #D4E6F1
One independent RX descriptor queue per
ingress port. Arms + starts exactly the
FIRST slot only -- see the note on
frer_poll_receive() below for why.
end note
RSW --> REP: FSP_SUCCESS

REP -> REP: wait for ETH0 + ETH1 link UP\n(30 s timeout, same reasoning as Sender)
REP -> PC: console: "[FRER] ETH0 link: UP  ETH1 link: UP (after N ms)"

REP -> RSW: frer_configure_recovery()\n-> ConfigureTable() + AddTableEntry() x2
note over REP, RSW #D4E6F1
Two L3 entries (one per ingress port), both
pointing at ONE shared sequence-recovery
context via p_frer_entry_cfg.p_sequence_recovery
-- this is what makes recovery compound
(cross-path) instead of two independent
per-path ones.
end note
RSW --> REP: FSP_SUCCESS
REP -> PC: console: "[FRER] L3 entries: 2  RX queues: Port0=N  Port1=M"
REP -> PC: console: "[FRER] Waiting for the companion Sender's replicated frame..."

== Run Loop: Sender (every FRER_SEND_PERIOD_MS = 100 ms) ==

loop forever, no stop condition
    SEP -> SSW: frer_send_one()\n-> SetDescriptor(FSINGLE) + StartDescriptorQueue()
    note right of SEP #D4E6F1
    Relies entirely on the matched L3 entry's
    own destination_ports for replication --
    never touches desc.info1_tx.fmt/dv/ipv
    directly.
    end note
    SSW --> SSW: Hardware replicates the one frame onto\nboth Port0 and Port1, inserting each\nmember stream's own R-TAG + sequence number
    SSW -> RSW: Member stream A (Port0->Port0, R-TAG seq=N)
    SSW -> RSW: Member stream B (Port1->Port1, R-TAG seq=N)

    opt every FRER_RATE_REPORT_EVERY (50) sends, ~5 s
        SEP -> PC: console: "[FRER] Sent N frames (~10 frames/s injection rate)"
        SEP -> PC: console: "[FRER] tx diag: submitted=.. skipped_busy=.. skipped_overflow=.."
        SEP -> SEP: re-poll ETH0/ETH1 link status
        opt a link is down
            SEP -> PC: console: "[FRER] WARNING: ETH0 link: .. ETH1 link: .. -- frames cannot flow on a down link"
        end opt
    end opt
end loop

== Run Loop: Receiver (every FRER_POLL_PERIOD_MS = 10 ms) ==

loop forever
    REP -> REP: frer_example_check_console()\n(non-blocking: any line toggles STOP<->RESTART)
    opt a line was typed while STOPPED
        REP -> RSW: frer_restart()\n-> Close() + Open() + redo RX queues + recovery entries
        note over REP, RSW #FFF9C4
        Only way to give an RX queue a fresh
        tail=0 without a board reset -- SetDescriptor()'s
        internal tail index is a confirmed WHOLE-LIFETIME
        counter for RX (never reset by Start(), unlike TX),
        so FRER_RX_DESC_NUM-1 = 99 frames/port is the
        total this queue can EVER capture between restarts.
        end note
        RSW --> REP: FSP_SUCCESS
        REP -> PC: console: "[FRER] RUNNING again, all counters reset to zero"
    end opt

    RSW --> RSW: Individual recovery (per-port integrity check,\nentries #1/#2) then shared sequence recovery\n(entry #0): first arrival of a sequence number\npasses, every later duplicate of it is discarded\nin hardware before reaching a GWCA RX queue
    REP -> RSW: frer_poll_receive(Port0)\n-> GetDescriptor()
    alt a frame is pending
        RSW --> REP: frame (R-TAG sequence number, length)
        REP -> PC: console: "[FRER] port0 sequence number:XXXX  length:N"
    else nothing pending yet
        RSW --> REP: false
    end alt
    REP -> RSW: frer_poll_receive(Port1)\n-> GetDescriptor()
    alt a frame is pending
        RSW --> REP: frame (R-TAG sequence number, length)
        REP -> PC: console: "[FRER] port1 sequence number:XXXX  length:N"
    else nothing pending yet
        RSW --> REP: false
    end alt

    opt every 1000 ms
        REP -> RSW: frer_get_l3_classification()\n-> R_MFWD->FWLTHFDCN0/1 (ingress ground truth)
        REP -> RSW: frer_get_hw_frer_counters()\n-> R_MFWD->FWFRPPCNi/FWFRDPCNi (recovery ground truth)
        REP -> PC: console: Periodic pipeline summary (every ~1 s)\n(ingress -> individual recovery -> sequence\nrecovery -> delivered to CPU) + VERDICT line
        REP -> REP: re-poll ETH0/ETH1 link status
        opt a link is down
            REP -> PC: console: "[FRER] WARNING: ETH0 link: .. ETH1 link: .. -- frames cannot flow on a down link"
        end opt
        opt a port just reached its 99-frame lifetime cap
            REP -> PC: console: "[FRER] NOTE: portN has reached its 99-frame lifetime capacity..."
        end opt
    end opt
end loop

@enduml
